@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.
   Guarded by DebugPageRenderTests (step 12). *@
@using Humans.Application.Extensions
@using Humans.Debug
@using Humans.Debug.Controllers
@using Humans.Debug.Models
@using Humans.Infrastructure.Logging
@using Humans.UI
@using Humans.UI.Models
@using Humans.UI.Models.Tables
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@* Debug carries no resource set of its own — every string on these pages is English
   developer copy (step 3b's "does the section have any keys" opens with no). The one
   localizer the section touches is SharedResource, and only as *data*: /Debug/Translations
   enumerates the whole shared set as a coverage gallery. DebugArchitectureTests pins that
   to SharedResource so a future page cannot quietly bind some third set. *@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@* A section can only addTagHelper against Humans.UI — a Shell-resident component renders
   as inert literal markup (step 6). <vc:human> is in Humans.UI already. *@
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Interfaces
